<title>AUSTRIA: Kuwait sees OPEC deal buoying prices.</title>
<headline>Kuwait sees OPEC deal buoying prices.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kuwaiti Oil Minister Isa al-Mazeedi said he thought the OPEC accord would keep prices strong and perhaps move them somewhat higher.</p>
<p>He told reporters that &quot;I see no reason why prices should not stay the same, if not a bit higher&quot;.</p>
<p>He said he was not worried about resumed Iraqi sales as they would involve &quot;a very insignificant amount of oil&quot;.</p>
<p>The minister said OPEC ministers had looked at demand forecasts that showed the world economies &quot;really growing&quot;</p>
<p>There had been no need to discuss over-production.</p>
<p>&quot;We will meet again in June and everyone will have enough time to review the situation then&quot;.</p>
</text>
